 Arms Race Is Reshaping Global Computing"}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":"16px","color":"#737373","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"July 8, 2026"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"AI in China"}]]}]]}],["$","img",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1200&q=80","alt":"ByteDance's $29 Billion AI Bet: How China's Quiet Infrastructure Arms Race Is Reshaping Global Computing","style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto","borderRadius":"12px","marginBottom":"48px"}}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1537531383496-f4749b8032cf?w=1200\""}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"  The Number That...\""}]]}],["$","hr","2",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","p","7",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*Photo by NASA on Unsplash*"}]]}],["$","hr","9",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","11",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Number That Changed the Conversation"}]]}],["$","p","13",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"On May 9, 2026, a Friday afternoon in Beijing, ByteDance executives gathered for what was supposed to be a routine budget review. CEO Liang Rubo walked in with a single slide. The number on it — "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"200 billion yuan"}],["$","span","2",{"children":" — made the room go silent."}]]}],["$","p","15",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"That figure, roughly "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"$$29.4 billion"}],["$","span","2",{"children":", represented ByteDance's revised AI infrastructure spending plan for 2026. Not revenue. Not total capex. Just AI infrastructure. It was a 25% increase from the 160 billion yuan the company had committed just six months earlier, and it effectively made ByteDance the single largest private AI investor in China — surpassing Tencent, Baidu, and every startup in the industry combined."}]]}],["$","p","17",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"But the real story wasn't the number itself. It was what the number represented: "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"China's AI infrastructure buildout has reached a scale that can no longer be ignored by the rest of the world."}]]}],["$","p","19",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"For years, Western analysts dismissed Chinese AI spending as \"catch-up investment\" — necessary, perhaps, but fundamentally reactive. The narrative was simple: US hyperscalers like Amazon, Google, and Microsoft were building the future; Chinese companies were scrambling to keep up with cheaper knock-offs and government subsidies."}]]}],["$","p","21",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"ByteDance's $29 billion check shatters that narrative. Because when you add up what China's top five tech companies are spending on AI infrastructure in 2026, the total approaches "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"$$80 billion"}],["$","span","2",{"children":". That's not catch-up money. That's competitive money. And in some categories — data center capacity, domestic chip deployment, and AI model inference volume — China is now moving faster than the US."}]]}],["$","hr","23",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","25",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"How We Got Here: The Infrastructure Timeline"}]]}],["$","p","27",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"To understand why ByteDance felt compelled to add another 40 billion yuan to its AI budget, you need to understand what happened in the six months between December 2025 and May 2026."}]]}],["$","p","29",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"In December 2025, ByteDance had planned to spend 160 billion yuan on AI — already a massive increase from the roughly 150 billion spent in 2025. The budget was split three ways: GPUs and accelerators for training and inference, memory chips (HBM3 and HBM4), and new data center capacity across Shanxi, Inner Mongolia, and other northern provinces where electricity is cheap and land is plentiful."}]]}],["$","p","31",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Then three things happened simultaneously."}]]}],["$","p","33",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"First, Doubao exploded."}],["$","span","1",{"children":" ByteDance's AI chatbot, which most Western observers had never heard of, surpassed 345 million monthly active users in early 2026. That made it the most-used AI app in China by a wide margin — ahead of Alibaba's Qwen, Tencent's Yuanbao, and even DeepSeek. Each of those users generates inference requests that require compute. Lots of compute. By March, ByteDance's internal estimates suggested Doubao alone would consume 40% more GPU capacity than originally planned."}]]}],["$","p","35",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Second, memory prices went vertical."}],["$","span","1",{"children":" HBM3 and HBM4 — the high-bandwidth memory that sits next to every AI accelerator — saw sustained price increases of 30-50% as global demand outstripped supply. Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron were all running at capacity, but the memory bottleneck meant that even if ByteDance could buy more GPUs, it couldn't necessarily power them. The 40 billion yuan increase was partly a simple price adjustment: the same hardware now cost more."}]]}],["$","p","37",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Third, and most strategically, the company made a decision about chips."}],["$","span","1",{"children":" ByteDance had historically been one of NVIDIA's largest Chinese customers. But tightening US export controls, combined with Beijing's increasingly explicit pressure to use domestic chips, forced a reassessment. The revised budget shifted a \"growing share\" toward domestically produced accelerators — primarily Huawei's Ascend series, but also ByteDance's own custom ASIC project, codenamed SeedChip, which is being developed in partnership with Samsung's foundry division."}]]}],["$","div","45",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Period"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"ByteDance AI Capex"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Key Driver"}]]}],["$","th","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Strategic Focus"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2024"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~80 billion yuan ($11B)"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Early Doubao scaling"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"NVIDIA H100/H200 acquisition"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2025"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"~150 billion yuan ($22B)"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Doubao 200M+ MAU"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Memory + GPU capacity expansion"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Dec 2025 Plan"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"160 billion yuan ($23B)"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Pre-2026 budget cycle"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Balanced domestic/imported split"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"May 2026 Revision"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"200 billion yuan ($29B)"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Doubao surge + memory prices"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Heavy domestic chip pivot"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","blockquote","47",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Source:"}],["$","span","1",{"children":" Financial Times, Bloomberg, SCMP, ByteDance internal reports (via sources)"}]]}]]}],["$","hr","48",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","50",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Global Context: China's $80B vs. America's $725B"}]]}],["$","p","52",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Putting ByteDance's $29 billion in perspective requires looking at the global AI infrastructure landscape. And here, the numbers tell a more nuanced story than simple \"China vs. America\" headlines suggest."}]]}],["$","p","54",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The four largest US hyperscalers — Amazon, Google, Meta, and Microsoft — are collectively spending approximately "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"$$725 billion"}],["$","span","2",{"children":" on capex in 2026, with the overwhelming majority going to AI infrastructure. Amazon alone is guiding to roughly $200 billion. That's seven times ByteDance's budget."}]]}],["$","p","56",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"But aggregate numbers can be misleading. When you look at AI-specific spending, the gap narrows. And when you look at AI spending as a percentage of revenue, or as a measure of strategic commitment, China starts to look different."}]]}],["$","div","68",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2p