, but compared to Amazon's $200 billion, the gap is still huge. Still, investing 24% of revenue into AI shows more determination than Alibaba or Tencent.\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","184",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"X (Twitter)"}]]}],["$","blockquote","186",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"ByteDance spending $29B on AI in 2026 while the US is spending $725B. The real question isn't who's spending more — it's who's spending smarter. China's inference-optimized infrastructure is built for scale, not just benchmarks.\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","187",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Xiaohongshu (小红书)"}]]}],["$","blockquote","191",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"在火山引擎工作，只能说这2000亿不是画饼，是真金白银在买卡、建机房、招工程师。每天处理的token量已经超过美国不少公司了。\""}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[]}],["$","p","2",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"Working at Volcano Engine — I can tell you this 200 billion isn't just hype. It's real money buying GPUs, building data centers, and hiring engineers. Our daily token volume already exceeds many US companies.\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","192",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Douban (豆瓣)"}]]}],["$","blockquote","196",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"又一个『中国威胁论』的素材。但说实话，当我们讨论AI基础设施时，总是忽略了一个事实：美国公司是为全球用户服务的，中国公司主要是服务中国用户。500亿日请求vs800亿，但用户基数差了多少？\""}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[]}],["$","p","2",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"Another piece of 'China threat' propaganda. But honestly, when we talk about AI infrastructure, we always ignore one fact: US companies serve global users, Chinese companies mainly serve Chinese users. 500B vs 800B daily requests — but what's the user base difference?\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","197",{"style":{"fontStyle":"italic","color":"#737373","textAlign":"center","margin":"8px 0 24px"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"GitHub"}]]}],["$","blockquote","199",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"The SeedChip project is interesting. If ByteDance can actually ship 350K custom ASICs in 2026, that's a massive deal. But Samsung 3nm yield rates for AI chips are still unproven. I'll believe it when I see the benchmarks.\""}]]}]]}],["$","p","200",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Weibo (微博)"}]]}],["$","blockquote","204",{"style":{"borderLeft":"4px solid #22d3ee","paddingLeft":"24px","margin":"24px 0","fontStyle":"italic","color":"#a3a3a3"},"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"字节跳动用2000亿告诉所有人：短视频只是入口，AI才是终局。这盘棋下得比大多数人想象的都要大。\""}]]}],["$","p","1",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[]}],["$","p","2",{"style":{"margin":"8px 0"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"ByteDance is telling everyone with 200 billion yuan: short video is just the entry point, AI is the endgame. They're playing a much bigger game than most people realize.\""}]]}]]}],["$","hr","205",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","h2","207",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Bottom Line"}]]}],["$","p","209",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"ByteDance's $29 billion AI investment is not just a budget line item. It's a signal — to competitors, to suppliers, to policymakers, and to the global tech industry — that China's AI infrastructure buildout has entered a new phase."}]]}],["$","p","211",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The first phase, from 2022 to 2024, was about catching up. Chinese companies bought NVIDIA chips, trained models, and released products that were competent but not exceptional."}]]}],["$","p","213",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The second phase, from 2024 to 2025, was about differentiation. DeepSeek proved Chinese models could match US performance at lower cost. Doubao proved Chinese AI apps could reach hundreds of millions of users. Zhipu and MiniMax proved Chinese AI companies could go public and succeed."}]]}],["$","p","215",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The third phase, which began in 2026, is about infrastructure dominance. ByteDance's 200 billion yuan is not just an investment in GPUs and data centers. It's an investment in the foundational layer of the next computing platform — the layer that will determine who controls AI in the 2030s."}]]}],["$","p","217",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"And here's the part that should make everyone pay attention: "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"ByteDance is not the only Chinese company making this bet."}],["$","span","2",{"children":" Alibaba is spending $52 billion over three years. Tencent is doubling its AI investment. Huawei is building a chip ecosystem from scratch. The NDRC is planning a national AI data center network that will span the entire country."}]]}],["$","p","219",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The race for AI infrastructure is not a sprint. It's a marathon. And China just laced up its running shoes."}]]}],["$","hr","221",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","p","223",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*Related articles:*"}]]}],["$","p","224",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- "}],["$","a","1",{"href":"/blog/china-ai-chip-renaissance-q1-2026/","style":{"color":"#22d3ee","textDecoration":"underline"},"children":"China's Triple Silicon Gambit: 75 Million AI Chips and the Road to AGI"}]]}],["$","p","225",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"- "}],["$","a","1",{"href":"/blog/bytedance-ai-gamble-gpu-kingpin-profit-drop/","style":{"color":"#22d3ee","textDecoration":"underline"},"children":"ByteDance's AI Obsession: From 70% Profit Plunge to GPU Kingpin"}]]}],["$","p","226",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},